    "q-99580": {
      "dom_id": "step-q99580",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$(-21)÷(-7)=$",
      "worked_solution": "We have to divide a negative number $(-21)$ by another negative number $(-7).$ So the result will be positive:\n\n$$\n(-21)÷(-7)=\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $21$ by $7$ without any signs: $21÷7=3.$ Therefore,  we get\n\n$$\n(-21)÷(-7)=3.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
