    "q-128420": {
      "dom_id": "step-q128420",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Expressed as a mixed number, $19÷(-6)=$",
      "worked_solution": "We have to divide a positive number $(19)$ by a negative one $(-6).$ So the result will be negative:\n\n$$\n19÷(-6)=-\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $19$ by $-6$ without any signs: $19÷6=3\\,\\frac{1}{6}.$ Therefore,  we get\n\n$$\n19÷(-6)=-3\\,\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$",
